1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,000
Right now, you feel the chair beneath you, or the mug in your hand.

2
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:09,250
Except according to physics, you have never actually touched anything in your entire life.

3
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:12,950
Nora: Hold on. I am literally poking this table right now.

4
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:19,900
Zoom in ten million times, and your fingertip stops hovering a fraction of a nanometer above the wood.

5
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:23,750
Every atom is wrapped in negatively charged electrons.

6
00:00:24,070 --> 00:00:29,250
Push yours toward the table, and those clouds repel each other like invisible magnets.

7
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:33,700
Nora: So technically, I am levitating right now. Honestly, pretty impressive.

8
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:41,700
What your nerves call solid is really that electromagnetic forcefield pressing your skin back before a single atom ever collides.

9
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:48,850
Which is very good news, because forcing two atomic nuclei to actually touch is called nuclear fusion.

10
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:52,650
Nora: Okay, hovering is great. Suddenly a huge fan of the gap.

11
00:00:53,150 --> 00:01:01,050
Yet across that tiny gulf, those invisible forces still carry warmth, weight, and every handshake you have ever felt.

12
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:05,150
Close enough to feel everything, without ever colliding.
